?source=iedfolrf0000001","evidence_url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/04/berkshire-hathaway-has-invested-23-billion-in-this/?source=iedfolrf0000001","evidence_label":"article","publisher":"The Motley Fool","match_tier":"high","evidence_document_id":null},{"in_base_irr":false,"confidence":"med","event_type":"management","impact_axis":"catalyst","source":"news","as_of":"2026-08-03","scope":"ticker","ref":"BRK.B","title":"Greg Abel Closed Berkshire Hathaway's Taylor Morrison Deal on July 24. Here's What Berkshire Owns Now.","claim":"Berkshire Hathaway completed its $8.5 billion acquisition of Taylor Morrison Home for $72.50 per share under new CEO Greg Abel. This is Berkshire's second homebuilder acquisition, positioning the conglomerate to capture multiple stages of the homebuilding process through its existing portfolio of building material and product companies. Despite current high mortgage rates, Berkshire is playing the long game, expecting to benefit when the housing market rebounds.","direction":"neutral","evidence_ref":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/03/abel-closed-berkshire-hathaways-taylor-morrison/?source=iedfolrf0000001","evidence_url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/03/abel-closed-berkshire-hathaways-taylor-morrison/?source=iedfolrf0000001","evidence_label":"article","publisher":"The Motley Fool","match_tier":"high","evidence_document_id":null},{"in_base_irr":false,"confidence":"med","event_type":"m_and_a","impact_axis":"catalyst","source":"news","as_of":"2026-08-03","scope":"ticker","ref":"BRK.B","title":"Greg Abel Is Spending Berkshire Hathaway's Cash on Whole Companies Instead of Stocks. Here's What That Changes for Shareholders.","claim":"Greg Abel, Berkshire Hathaway's new CEO, is shifting the company's investment strategy toward acquiring whole businesses rather than stocks. With nearly $400 billion in cash, Abel has spent less than $3 billion on stock purchases while acquiring Taylor Morrison for $6.8 billion and completing the OxyChem purchase for $9.7 billion. This approach reflects Abel's preference for long-term operational control over portfolio trading, as he finds greater value in whole companies than in the current richly-valued stock market.","direction":"neutral","evidence_ref":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/03/greg-abel-is-spending-berkshire-hathaways-cash-on/?source=iedfolrf0000001","evidence_url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/03/greg-abel-is-spending-berkshire-hathaways-cash-on/?source=iedfolrf0000001","evidence_label":"article","publisher":"The Motley Fool","match_tier":"high","evidence_document_id":null},{"in_base_irr":false,"confidence":"med","event_type":"m_and_a","impact_axis":"catalyst","source":"news","as_of":"2026-08-03","scope":"ticker","ref":"BRK.B","title":"Greg Abel's Berkshire Hathaway: What the Next Decade Could Look Like","claim":"Greg Abel, the new CEO of Berkshire Hathaway following Warren Buffett's retirement, acquired homebuilder Taylor Morrison for $6.8 billion. The deal signals a shift in management style—Abel plans to be more hands-on than Buffett, integrating Berkshire's housing businesses into a unified platform. This represents an evolution rather than a radical change, with Abel expected to leverage Berkshire's scale for acquisitions while improving internal operations over the next decade.","direction":"neutral","evidence_ref":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/02/greg-abels-berkshire-hathaway-what-the-next-decade/?source=iedfolrf0000001","evidence_url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/02/greg-abels-berkshire-hathaway-what-the-next-decade/?source=iedfolrf0000001","evidence_label":"article","publisher":"The Motley Fool","match_tier":"high","evidence_document_id":null},{"in_base_irr":false,"confidence":"med","event_type":"research_source","impact_axis":"variant_view","source":"third_party","as_of":"2026-08-02","scope":"ticker","ref":"BRK.B","title":"&#8194 (+2) — SC 13D/A","claim":"&#8194 (+2) — SC 13D/A (context; a